"donor_lfcse":0.166549,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0030764}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000142534","module":"greenyellow","kme":0.289237,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.56571,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000142534","module":"turquoise","kme":0.345007,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.572565,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000142534","module":"turquoise","kme":0.279834,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.446504,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000142534","module":"turquoise","kme":0.160945,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.704234,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000142534","module":"turquoise","kme":0.206027,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.415372,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000142534","entrez_id":["6205"],"uniprot":["P62280"],"ncbi_summary":"Ribosomes, the organelles that catalyze protein synthesis, consist of a small 40S subunit and a large 60S subunit. Together these subunits are composed of 4 RNA species and approximately 80 structurally distinct proteins. This gene encodes a member of the S17P family of ribosomal proteins that is a component of the 40S subunit. This gene is co-transcribed with the small nucleolar RNA gene U35B, which is located in the third intron. As is typical for genes encoding ribosomal proteins, there are multiple processed pseudogenes of this gene dispersed throughout the genome. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2012].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P62280","text":"Component of the small ribosomal subunit. The ribosome is a large ribonucleoprotein complex responsible for the synthesis of proteins in the cell. Part of the small subunit (SSU) processome, first precursor of the small eukaryotic ribosomal subunit. During the assembly of the SSU processome in the nucleolus, many ribosome biogenesis factors, an RNA chaperone and ribosomal proteins associate with the nascent pre-rRNA and work in concert to generate RNA folding, modifications, rearrangements and cleavage as well as targeted degradation of pre-ribosomal RNA by the RNA exosome (PubMed:34516797)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}